WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.110 --> 00:06.111
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

3
00:06.194 --> 00:08.030
THERE IS NO RELATION TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

4
00:08.530 --> 00:11.199
EPISODE 4

5
00:11.992 --> 00:13.994
[alarm beeping]

6
00:16.121 --> 00:17.122
[alarm stops]

7
00:29.134 --> 00:30.427
How'd I get here?

8
00:32.888 --> 00:34.514
I'll trust you, Yubin.

9
00:34.598 --> 00:36.683
[in Korean] You can trust me.

10
00:38.060 --> 00:39.603
[in English] I can trust him, right?

11
00:42.522 --> 00:44.358
[Yubin] Karin! Are you awake?

12
00:44.983 --> 00:47.486
-Uh… [sighs] -[Yubin] Breakfast is ready.

13
00:49.404 --> 00:50.405
[sighs]

14
00:52.657 --> 00:53.658
[sighs]

15
01:08.382 --> 01:09.633
[in Korean] All done.

16
01:17.391 --> 01:18.475
[in English] Karin.

17
01:19.059 --> 01:20.185
Why did I hide?

18
01:20.268 --> 01:21.269
Karin?

19
01:25.899 --> 01:27.651
[stammers, chuckles]

20
01:27.734 --> 01:29.736
[puffing]

21
01:32.197 --> 01:34.783
-It's early. What are you doing? -Huh?

22
01:34.866 --> 01:40.330
Um… Nothing. Airing out… [sighing]

23
01:40.414 --> 01:41.748
[chuckles]

24
01:43.041 --> 01:44.209
Your breakfast.

25
01:45.502 --> 01:46.670
Come and eat.

26
02:02.769 --> 02:04.729
Um… [sighs]

27
02:08.859 --> 02:10.110
[in Korean] Yesterday.

28
02:10.861 --> 02:12.404
[in English] Hmm? What about it?

29
02:13.113 --> 02:14.114
Uh…

30
02:15.532 --> 02:17.534
Oh, did something happen?

31
02:20.871 --> 02:21.872
[in Korean] You…

32
02:28.420 --> 02:29.546
snored like crazy.

33
02:30.756 --> 02:32.340
It was so loud.

34
02:32.424 --> 02:33.967
[in English] I do not snore, okay?

35
02:34.050 --> 02:35.677
[♪ playful music playing]

36
02:37.429 --> 02:38.430
I mean…

37
02:39.431 --> 02:44.978
Maybe a little bit. Not always. It's just when I'm really tired.

38
02:45.061 --> 02:47.063
[in Korean] All right. [in English] Hurry up and eat.

39
02:49.483 --> 02:50.817
Thanks for the meal.

40
02:58.617 --> 02:59.868
Hmm?

41
02:59.951 --> 03:00.952
What is this?

42
03:01.870 --> 03:02.996
I've never had this before.

43
03:03.079 --> 03:05.332
-You like it? Good. -Mm-hmm.

44
03:05.415 --> 03:08.627
What you're eating is a Korean-style toast.

45
03:08.710 --> 03:10.712
Mmm…

46
03:10.796 --> 03:12.881
-It's great! -[in Korean] Help yourself.

47
03:12.964 --> 03:14.508
There's another one over there.

48
03:15.217 --> 03:17.052
[in English] Hmm? What about you?

49
03:17.135 --> 03:19.221
[in Korean] I have to go somewhere real quick.

50
03:19.304 --> 03:20.639
[Karin, in English] Hmm?

51
03:20.722 --> 03:22.682
Where to? And for how long?

52
03:23.433 --> 03:24.434
[Yubin chuckles]

53
03:25.143 --> 03:26.144
[in Korean] Boss,

54
03:27.437 --> 03:28.813
you care about me that much?

55
03:28.897 --> 03:29.898
[inhales sharply]

56
03:29.981 --> 03:31.441
[in English] No, um…

57
03:31.525 --> 03:34.110
I have to keep track of your hours as your employer and all.

58
03:34.194 --> 03:38.448
[chuckles, speaks Korean] They're setting up our booth today.

59
03:39.741 --> 03:41.326
I should go take a look.

60
03:42.827 --> 03:44.204
[sighs]

61
03:45.080 --> 03:46.081
Right…

62
03:49.292 --> 03:50.293
[in English] I'll be back.

63
03:52.337 --> 03:54.548
Mmm. Have a good day.

64
03:55.257 --> 03:56.258
[sighs]

65
04:02.347 --> 04:03.765
"I'll be back…"

66
04:09.771 --> 04:11.523
[sighs]

67
04:11.606 --> 04:12.691
[in Korean] Sheesh… [sighs]

68
04:13.984 --> 04:15.610
What the heck was that?

69
04:16.152 --> 04:18.738
How can someone be so cute so early in the morning?

70
04:19.698 --> 04:22.701
Is she planning on being so cute all day long?

71
04:22.784 --> 04:26.162
-[phone buzzing] -Man, hope she didn't hear that.

72
04:28.415 --> 04:30.166
HYEJIN

73
04:31.084 --> 04:32.419
Hello?

74
04:33.044 --> 04:34.546
[Hyejin] I got a call from Sia.

75
04:35.463 --> 04:37.299
Han Sia?

76
04:37.382 --> 04:40.802
She asked about that land.

77
04:40.886 --> 04:43.471
How does Sia know about my land?

78
04:44.139 --> 04:47.350
You know her family is in the resort business.

79
04:47.434 --> 04:49.811
Sounds like she's interested.

80
04:50.812 --> 04:52.814
Why don't you meet with her once?

81
04:53.523 --> 04:54.524
Yeah, sure.

82
04:54.608 --> 04:55.692
When are you coming back?

83
04:56.276 --> 04:57.277
[grunts]

84
04:58.987 --> 05:00.447
The thing is…

85
05:02.324 --> 05:03.575
[grunts, sighs]

86
05:04.159 --> 05:06.077
I need a little time…

87
05:06.745 --> 05:08.371
You could fly back soon.

88
05:08.455 --> 05:09.998
Want me to book your flight?

89
05:10.081 --> 05:12.709
No, no need. Just…

90
05:13.627 --> 05:15.962
I'll come back in a few days.

91
05:17.547 --> 05:20.759
This is a huge opportunity.

92
05:20.842 --> 05:23.595
Don't wait around.

93
05:23.678 --> 05:26.473
I won't. I'm hanging up.

94
05:27.223 --> 05:28.224
[phone beeps]

95
05:31.811 --> 05:32.854
[sighs]

96
05:45.033 --> 05:48.453
[in English] Mari, hi. I got us something that'll fix our hangovers!

97
05:48.536 --> 05:49.537
RAMYEON

98
05:49.621 --> 05:51.456
Oh, I'll boil the water then.

99
06:07.639 --> 06:10.392
-So, um… Mari… Can I… -[Mari] Hmm?

100
06:11.851 --> 06:14.896
Can I consider today our day one?

101
06:15.522 --> 06:16.690
Day one of what?

102
06:16.773 --> 06:19.109
Like, of us becoming official?

103
06:19.192 --> 06:20.527
Yeah.

104
06:21.027 --> 06:23.321
Yesterday, did you forget that we…

105
06:24.823 --> 06:26.491
Forget that we what?

106
06:26.574 --> 06:28.576
[thunderclap]

107
06:30.036 --> 06:32.622
Wait, don't you remember what we did?

108
06:34.499 --> 06:38.878
-[♪ upbeat music playing] -[both singing last note]

109
06:38.962 --> 06:40.171
[♪ music ends]

110
06:40.255 --> 06:42.257
[both chuckling, exclaiming]

111
06:44.676 --> 06:45.677
We're doing great!

112
06:45.760 --> 06:48.054
Uh-huh. Thanks to us and all our hard work,

113
06:48.138 --> 06:50.432
everyone's gonna line up for Karin's booth!

114
06:50.515 --> 06:51.850
Thank you for all your training.

115
06:51.933 --> 06:53.893
[both chuckling]

116
06:53.977 --> 06:56.396
Oh. [gasps]

117
06:58.732 --> 06:59.983
[gasps]

118
07:03.445 --> 07:04.696
[sighs]

119
07:07.907 --> 07:09.451
Wow.

120
07:10.869 --> 07:13.079
Kunam… [gasps]

121
07:15.039 --> 07:16.040
Uh…

122
07:16.958 --> 07:18.543
Don't you think that…

123
07:19.753 --> 07:22.213
this is kind of romantic?

124
07:22.756 --> 07:24.674
-Huh? -It's time.

125
07:26.176 --> 07:27.594
I'm ready for this.

126
07:42.066 --> 07:43.359
[Kunam] Mari…

127
07:43.443 --> 07:44.819
I really…

128
07:46.529 --> 07:47.822
really like you a lot.

129
07:51.576 --> 07:53.578
[kettle whistling]

130
07:59.667 --> 08:01.294
[Kunam] Our romantic hug.

131
08:01.878 --> 08:03.505
-Th-that was… -Just because we hugged,

132
08:03.588 --> 08:06.674
it doesn't mean that we're automatically dating.

133
08:07.258 --> 08:11.429
If it did, I would've been married over a hundred times by now.

134
08:11.513 --> 08:13.389
[sighs]

135
08:14.224 --> 08:18.686
We locked eyes romantically. You felt it too. I know you did.

136
08:20.855 --> 08:22.774
It wasn't just me, right?

137
08:24.359 --> 08:25.735
[sighs]

138
08:25.819 --> 08:27.529
I didn't feel anything.

139
08:27.612 --> 08:29.739
Well, other than the alcohol.

140
08:32.283 --> 08:34.202
Well, I… I felt it.

141
08:34.285 --> 08:35.662
[Mari] Ah, come on.

142
08:36.538 --> 08:37.539
Relax a little.

143
08:37.622 --> 08:40.041
You take everything way too seriously.

144
08:42.043 --> 08:43.044
Want some takuan?

145
08:44.796 --> 08:45.922
I'm taking these.

146
08:49.634 --> 08:50.969
[door closes]

147
08:51.886 --> 08:52.887
[Mari sighs]

148
08:57.016 --> 08:58.351
[sighs]

149
08:59.853 --> 09:00.937
[in Korean] Bro.

150
09:02.522 --> 09:03.523
Hey…

151
09:07.735 --> 09:09.737
[both slurping]

152
09:13.491 --> 09:14.993
[sighs]

153
09:15.076 --> 09:16.286
Soup sure goes down easy

154
09:18.454 --> 09:19.539
even on a heavy heart.

155
09:20.165 --> 09:22.500
Being Korean is about consuming food.

156
09:22.584 --> 09:23.710
[sighs]

157
09:23.793 --> 09:24.836
[sighs]

158
09:26.087 --> 09:28.548
Were you hiding these from me?

159
09:29.174 --> 09:31.426
[grunts] These are Mari's favorites, so… [chuckles]

160
09:33.094 --> 09:34.554
Selfish guy.

161
09:34.637 --> 09:36.264
Love comes before friendship.

162
09:40.268 --> 09:42.395
Should we even be thinking about love in our situation?

163
09:42.478 --> 09:44.856
I don't know about you, but I'm going to give it my best.

164
09:44.939 --> 09:47.859
[scoffs] I can't just not go back.

165
09:47.942 --> 09:49.319
I'll never give up.

166
09:49.402 --> 09:53.031
Anyway, I have stuff to take care of.

167
09:53.114 --> 09:54.490
[Kunam] You're right.

168
09:54.574 --> 09:56.492
I have to sort things out

169
09:56.576 --> 09:59.662
and think about how to show her all my charms.

170
10:01.372 --> 10:02.665
Good luck.

171
10:04.375 --> 10:05.543
[sighs]

172
10:26.689 --> 10:27.690
[Karin chuckles]

173
10:30.485 --> 10:31.611
[in English] There it is.

174
10:32.946 --> 10:34.405
[chuckles]

175
10:36.699 --> 10:38.159
[chuckles]

176
10:38.243 --> 10:39.494
Hey, Yubin. Come here.

177
10:39.577 --> 10:41.663
Come look at this! [chuckles]

178
10:41.746 --> 10:43.289
The sugar levels have finally risen.

179
10:43.957 --> 10:45.625
-Look at that. -[in Korean] Let's see.

180
10:46.376 --> 10:47.377
[chuckles]

181
10:48.127 --> 10:49.128
[in English] Well?

182
10:49.212 --> 10:51.339
-[in Korean] Are you that happy? -So very happy!

183
10:51.422 --> 10:53.841
-[chuckles] "So very happy"? -So very happy!

184
10:53.925 --> 10:55.051
[both chuckle]

185
10:55.134 --> 10:56.386
-"So very happy"? -Uh-huh.

186
10:56.469 --> 10:59.013
[in English] Also, that strawberry I've been working on, it bloomed.

187
10:59.097 --> 11:00.181
-Mmm. -Come look.

188
11:01.975 --> 11:04.018
Come on! Let's go!

189
11:04.102 --> 11:06.312
-[chuckles] -[Karin] Hurry up!

190
11:10.358 --> 11:11.985
-See? Ta-da! -Ah.

191
11:12.068 --> 11:13.653
Wow.

192
11:13.736 --> 11:14.904
[chuckles] Aren't they pretty?

193
11:16.364 --> 11:17.365
Mm-hmm.

194
11:17.991 --> 11:19.450
-Very pretty. -Mm-hmm.

195
11:20.660 --> 11:22.745
-They're cute. -Mm-hmm. I agree.

196
11:27.542 --> 11:29.085
[in Korean] Do these flowers… Ah.

197
11:32.630 --> 11:34.674
Do these flowers have a meaning too?

198
11:35.258 --> 11:36.968
[in English] Mm-hmm. Of course.

199
11:37.051 --> 11:39.804
[chuckles] All flowers have meaning.

200
11:40.805 --> 11:41.889
[In Korean] What is it?

201
11:44.851 --> 11:47.020
[in English] Love and respect.

202
11:48.688 --> 11:49.689
LOVE AND RESPECT

203
11:49.772 --> 11:50.815
[Yubin] Oh.

204
11:52.275 --> 11:54.986
-Love and respect. -Respect.

205
11:55.069 --> 11:56.112
Mm-hmm.

206
11:57.155 --> 11:58.656
[chuckles] What is it in Korean?

207
12:03.536 --> 12:05.913
[in Korean] Love and respect.

208
12:07.248 --> 12:09.709
Love and respect.

209
12:09.792 --> 12:12.420
-Yeah. Love and respect. -Respect.

210
12:12.503 --> 12:13.755
[chuckles]

211
12:15.423 --> 12:17.759
Love and respect.

212
12:18.885 --> 12:20.887
Love and respect.

213
12:20.970 --> 12:22.138
-Yes. -Mmm.

214
12:24.932 --> 12:26.559
Love and respect.

215
12:50.291 --> 12:51.292
[sighs]

216
12:58.925 --> 13:01.469
THE SIXTH GREEN NOVA CORPORATION FESTA

217
13:01.552 --> 13:03.930
WHERE TOMORROW'S AGRICULTURE BEGINS

218
13:09.560 --> 13:10.561
SUEYASU FARM

219
13:10.645 --> 13:11.896
WITH AN AUTHENTIC ESPRESSO MACHINE

220
13:11.979 --> 13:14.273
-[in English] Good morning. -Good morning.

221
13:14.357 --> 13:15.858
MIZUMORI VILLAGE

222
13:25.368 --> 13:26.369
Good morning.

223
13:26.452 --> 13:29.705
WHERE TOMORROW'S AGRICULTURE BEGINS

224
13:29.789 --> 13:31.582
[chattering]

225
13:36.671 --> 13:37.672
[seller] Hello there.

226
13:37.755 --> 13:39.424
-Good morning. -Good morning.

227
13:40.258 --> 13:42.343
The day's finally here. [sighs]

228
13:43.177 --> 13:44.720
You've worked hard.

229
13:44.804 --> 13:46.889
-You've worked really hard too, Yubin. -[grunts]

230
13:47.932 --> 13:51.602
This year, I'll sweep the competition and get their backing.

231
13:52.687 --> 13:57.275
And then, Charo Island's products will be sold all throughout Japan, right?

232
13:57.817 --> 13:59.902
-[chuckles] That's right. -[chuckling]

233
14:04.532 --> 14:05.867
This is…

234
14:07.285 --> 14:10.413
CHARO ISLAND HARVESTING EXPERIENCE

235
14:32.310 --> 14:34.770
[Yubin chuckles] Uh…

236
14:35.897 --> 14:37.523
Well, what do you think?

237
14:39.275 --> 14:40.568
It's amazing.

238
14:45.114 --> 14:46.324
[grunts]

239
14:46.407 --> 14:49.327
[in Korean] I wanted to recreate the field you work on

240
14:49.410 --> 14:54.248
and let everyone here see it.

241
14:57.418 --> 15:00.463
[chuckles, speaks in English] I think you did a great job.

242
15:01.172 --> 15:03.007
This is just wonderful!

243
15:03.758 --> 15:05.092
I'm glad.

244
15:06.093 --> 15:07.386
[chuckles]

245
15:07.470 --> 15:11.974
[fans squealing, chuckling]

246
15:12.058 --> 15:15.519
Oh. Sleepyhead's island went all out.

247
15:15.603 --> 15:19.190
-Wow, more than I expected for sure. -[fans giggling]

248
15:19.273 --> 15:23.152
Too bad you put in all that effort because you'll be crushed next to me.

249
15:23.236 --> 15:25.988
-[fans squeal] -[Reiji] Wanna see it, huh?

250
15:26.864 --> 15:28.032
[fan] Oh, yay!

251
15:28.115 --> 15:30.243
Ta-da!

252
15:30.326 --> 15:32.036
[fans squealing]

253
15:39.585 --> 15:41.712
[in Korean] He's the worst.

254
15:43.130 --> 15:44.840
[in English] Word's getting around

255
15:44.924 --> 15:48.302
you said you're taking home the win this year, yeah?

256
15:49.011 --> 15:51.097
Good luck. I mean that, you know?

257
15:51.180 --> 15:52.765
Like, can't you wait till after?

258
15:52.848 --> 15:54.475
[fans squealing]

259
15:54.558 --> 15:55.893
Okay, who wants it?

260
15:56.727 --> 15:59.397
-You can all have one when we're done. -[fan] Oh, my God, really?

261
15:59.480 --> 16:01.565
[PA system chiming]

262
16:01.649 --> 16:04.151
[moderator on PA] We want to thank everyone for your patience.

263
16:04.694 --> 16:09.031
The Sixth Green Nova Corporation FESTA is now open to the public.

264
16:09.115 --> 16:10.366
[seller] Thank you.

265
16:11.200 --> 16:12.910
[moderator] Vote for your favorite Booth of the Day

266
16:12.994 --> 16:15.496
on the board in the middle of our venue.

267
16:15.579 --> 16:16.580
We're counting on your vote.

268
16:16.664 --> 16:18.124
IRO ISLAND - CHARO ISLAND AOBA VILLAGE

269
16:18.207 --> 16:22.128
Thank you for coming, and please enjoy all that our FESTA has to offer.

270
16:22.795 --> 16:24.922
-[child] Look at these strawberries. -[Karin] Thank you so much.

271
16:25.006 --> 16:26.007
They're pretty.

272
16:26.090 --> 16:27.883
-Can I take one? -Hey, be careful.

273
16:29.051 --> 16:32.638
-Can I have some strawberries? -Oh. Sure. Thank you.

274
16:32.722 --> 16:33.848
[Yubin] Thank you very much…

275
16:33.931 --> 16:36.475
-Here you are. -Yay! Yay!

276
16:36.559 --> 16:38.602
[Yubin] Can I show you? [in Korean] Go like this.

277
16:39.979 --> 16:40.980
[Karin chuckles]

278
16:41.689 --> 16:44.734
[in English] Wanna try? [in Korean] Go like this. [chuckles]

279
16:44.817 --> 16:46.110
[child, in English] Thank you.

280
16:46.193 --> 16:47.945
[Yubin] Thank you for stopping by.

281
16:48.029 --> 16:49.572
-[visitor] Thank you. -[Yubin chuckles]

282
16:49.655 --> 16:51.115
[both chuckle]

283
16:52.491 --> 16:54.493
[fans clamoring]

284
16:55.494 --> 16:57.163
[fan] Oh, I would love to have one of those.

285
16:57.246 --> 16:58.748
-Thanks very much. -Oh.

286
16:58.831 --> 16:59.957
[exclaims]

287
17:00.041 --> 17:02.585
-Thank you. -I'm most excited to be here.

288
17:02.668 --> 17:04.712
Wow, thank you. Thanks.

289
17:04.795 --> 17:08.174
Wow, thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.

290
17:08.257 --> 17:11.052
They're going fast. Thank you. I'm counting on you.

291
17:11.135 --> 17:13.262
-Yep. Thanks! -[fan] Oh, wait. Can I get a picture?

292
17:13.346 --> 17:15.014
[Mari] Karin!

293
17:16.265 --> 17:17.600
[chuckles]

294
17:18.100 --> 17:19.727
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

295
17:22.188 --> 17:23.439
Mari.

296
17:25.232 --> 17:27.568
-[Mari] Look who I found! [giggles] -[chattering]

297
17:27.651 --> 17:29.862
-[villagers laughing] -[villager] Karin, over here.

298
17:29.945 --> 17:31.697
[all] Hi! [laughing]

299
17:31.781 --> 17:32.907
We made it.

300
17:32.990 --> 17:34.533
[Mari] We're here! [chuckling]

301
17:34.617 --> 17:36.577
[all exclaiming]

302
17:36.661 --> 17:38.996
-Hi! Oh! -[laughing continues]

303
17:39.080 --> 17:43.376
Karin, our booth is the cutest booth out of everyone's.

304
17:43.459 --> 17:46.003
-[chuckles] Yeah. -This had to have been so much work.

305
17:46.087 --> 17:47.088
Not at all.

306
17:47.171 --> 17:49.632
-[villager] We're all very proud. -Ah, you're too sweet. Thanks so much.

307
17:49.715 --> 17:53.344
Yubin, thank you for designing this booth. It's so charming.

308
17:53.427 --> 17:55.805
-Oh, yes, thank you. Thank you, sir. -[villagers] Thank you.

309
17:55.888 --> 17:57.682
Yes, very nice…

310
17:57.765 --> 18:00.351
Why don't we all take a group photo together, huh?

311
18:00.434 --> 18:02.144
-Oh, of course. -That's a great idea.

312
18:02.228 --> 18:03.312
Everybody come here.

313
18:03.396 --> 18:05.064
-Over here. -Come on.

314
18:05.147 --> 18:06.148
Come on.

315
18:06.232 --> 18:08.401
-This way. This way. -[Karin] Ah…

316
18:08.484 --> 18:10.403
-Thank you. -Everybody get in.

317
18:10.486 --> 18:11.737
This way.

318
18:11.821 --> 18:14.365
-[in Korean] I'm taking the photo! -[in English] Yes, right here.

319
18:14.448 --> 18:16.033
Yubin, get in it.

320
18:16.575 --> 18:18.411
[in Korean] Yubin, get in here.

321
18:19.328 --> 18:21.539
-[in English] Yubin. Yubin! -Come join us!

322
18:21.622 --> 18:24.917
[all] Come, come! [chuckling]

323
18:25.000 --> 18:27.670
-Hurry, up! Come on! -Come, come!

324
18:27.753 --> 18:29.338
-Over here. -Come in, come in!

325
18:29.422 --> 18:30.423
Right here, right here.

326
18:30.506 --> 18:33.175
-Come on. Right here. -Come in here, Yubin.

327
18:33.259 --> 18:36.053
Oh! Come on. Come on!

328
18:36.137 --> 18:38.472
Don't be shy. Come on!

329
18:38.556 --> 18:40.641
[chief] Sorry, but can you take a photo?

330
18:42.601 --> 18:45.020
I'm a little busy right now but…

331
18:45.104 --> 18:47.523
Ready? Say cheese. Three, two, one…

332
18:47.606 --> 18:50.234
-Nice. Huh? -Not with you.

333
18:54.864 --> 18:55.990
Don't you know who I am?

334
18:56.073 --> 18:58.200
Are you being serious? I don't have time for that.

335
18:58.284 --> 19:00.661
[snarling]

336
19:01.537 --> 19:03.080
[high-pitched whimpering]

337
19:03.164 --> 19:06.250
Oh, yeah, fine. Yeah. I'll do it. I'll do it. Yeah. Okay, I got it.

338
19:06.333 --> 19:08.043
Squish together, everybody.

339
19:08.127 --> 19:09.253
All right, move in.

340
19:09.336 --> 19:10.796
Little bit tighter together.

341
19:11.964 --> 19:12.965
Closer.

342
19:13.048 --> 19:15.509
I can't see the people in the back.

343
19:15.593 --> 19:16.886
All right, that's good.

344
19:16.969 --> 19:18.179
Okay, smile!

345
19:18.262 --> 19:20.639
Three, two, one… cheese.

346
19:21.891 --> 19:26.312
[shutter clicking]

347
19:28.522 --> 19:31.609
[♪ upbeat song playing]

348
19:31.692 --> 19:36.155
We have a lot of tasty food here at our Charo Island booth. [chuckles]

349
19:36.238 --> 19:37.364
It's delicious.

350
19:37.448 --> 19:38.616
Hi there.

351
19:43.204 --> 19:44.205
It's delicious, right?

352
19:44.288 --> 19:47.208
-Mmm, mmm. -[in Korean] Are you Korean?

353
19:48.125 --> 19:49.835
[Kunam] Oh. Why do you ask?

354
19:49.919 --> 19:51.754
I heard you speaking Korean.

355
19:51.837 --> 19:53.088
Your Korean is really good.

356
19:53.172 --> 19:55.549
[visitor chuckles] I studied it.

357
19:55.633 --> 19:57.593
-Your pronunciation's on point. -[chuckling]

358
19:57.676 --> 20:01.680
[Kunam] If you don't mind, please vote for us for Booth of the Day.

359
20:01.764 --> 20:03.140
[visitor] Okay, we will.

360
20:03.224 --> 20:04.642
[in English] We appreciate that.

361
20:04.725 --> 20:06.685
-[in Korean] Thank you. -Thank you so much.

362
20:06.769 --> 20:07.978
[in English] Thank you.

363
20:10.898 --> 20:12.274
What's wrong?

364
20:12.358 --> 20:13.692
Are you tired?

365
20:14.902 --> 20:15.903
No.

366
20:16.904 --> 20:18.030
I'm totally fine.

367
20:23.244 --> 20:24.578
You're popular.

368
20:25.871 --> 20:26.914
Looks like it.

369
20:28.165 --> 20:30.835
Charo Island's products are perfect.

370
20:31.377 --> 20:32.962
It seems like everyone thinks that.

371
20:34.505 --> 20:37.675
-We welcome you to Charo Island's booth! -[chuckles]

372
20:38.551 --> 20:40.845
[both] Try our delicious samples!

373
20:40.928 --> 20:43.013
Sweet potatoes and strawberries!

374
20:43.097 --> 20:44.682
Uh, coming through.

375
20:48.060 --> 20:49.478
[grunts] Here, sweet potatoes!

376
20:49.562 --> 20:50.688
[Karin] Thank you.

377
20:51.814 --> 20:53.566
-Wow. -Wow.

378
20:54.358 --> 20:55.985
-[in Korean] Here. -[Kunam] We're back.

379
20:56.068 --> 20:58.279
-[Karin, Yubin] Ah. -You should make a round, bro.

380
20:59.321 --> 21:01.699
-Are you sure? -[Kunam] Yeah, we've got it from here.

381
21:01.782 --> 21:03.826
[in English] There's some time before the judging starts.

382
21:03.909 --> 21:05.411
You two should take a look around.

383
21:06.078 --> 21:07.663
[sighs] Great idea.

384
21:08.163 --> 21:09.290
[in Korean] Let's go, let's go.

385
21:09.373 --> 21:10.749
-[in English] Let's go. -[Karin yelps]

386
21:10.833 --> 21:13.586
All right. I'll leave it to you then. We'll be back in a minute.

387
21:13.669 --> 21:16.338
-Enjoy! Bye bye. -Thanks so much! Thank you!

388
21:18.299 --> 21:19.550
-[Mari] Hmm. -[Kunam] Hmm.

389
21:21.093 --> 21:22.094
[sighs]

390
21:22.177 --> 21:23.512
-[in Korean] Let's go! -Let's go!

391
21:24.013 --> 21:26.932
[villagers cheering]

392
21:27.016 --> 21:32.771
-[in English] Let's do our best! Yeah! -Charo Island!

393
21:32.855 --> 21:34.690
-[chanting] Charo Island! Charo Island! -Kumquats!

394
21:34.773 --> 21:37.026
Kumquats. Our team needs to chant. Over here.

395
21:37.109 --> 21:39.236
-Come on, hurry up! -Charo Island! Charo Island!

396
21:39.320 --> 21:41.822
-Hey, Iro Island! Iro Island! -[competitors chanting]

397
21:41.906 --> 21:44.325
-Charo Island! -[Reiji] Iro Island!

398
21:44.408 --> 21:46.827
-Come on! Louder! -Iro Island!

399
21:46.911 --> 21:50.873
-Louder! Iro! Iro! -Charo Island!

400
21:50.956 --> 21:52.791
[Kunam] Do your best!

401
21:52.875 --> 21:55.085
-Oh, hi, Mr. Iguchi. -[Mr. Iguchi] Hi, it's been a while.

402
21:55.169 --> 21:57.421
-I can't believe how long it's been. -[Mr. Iguchi] How are you?

403
21:57.504 --> 21:59.173
Oh. Ooh!

404
21:59.256 --> 22:00.841
-Ooh. -How is it? It's pretty hefty.

405
22:00.925 --> 22:02.176
Chief! How are you?

406
22:02.259 --> 22:03.886
-I haven't seen you in forever. -Oh, Karin!

407
22:03.969 --> 22:05.471
-How are things? -It's so good to see you.

408
22:05.554 --> 22:08.766
-Hi! You remember me? -Oh! Oh! Karin, hi!

409
22:08.849 --> 22:10.267
-Everything well, Ms. Koga? -Mmm, great.

410
22:10.351 --> 22:12.561
-The tomatoes are so vibrant. -[Koga] Mmm.

411
22:12.645 --> 22:16.398
[chief] Oh, Karin. Would you like to try a sample for yourself?

412
22:16.482 --> 22:18.275
-[Karin] Oh, can I? Thank you. -[chief] Of course.

413
22:18.359 --> 22:19.818
-Yubin. -[Yubin] Huh?

414
22:19.902 --> 22:20.945
-Tomatoes. -[chief] Welcome.

415
22:21.028 --> 22:22.655
-Mmm, good. -[Yubin] Mmm.

416
22:22.738 --> 22:25.157
[Koga] Karin. Why don't we get a photo

417
22:25.240 --> 22:26.533
-since you're here? -A photo?

418
22:26.617 --> 22:28.160
-[Yubin, Karin] Pose? -[chief] Nice.

419
22:28.243 --> 22:29.787
-[Koga] Something cute. -Like this.

420
22:29.870 --> 22:31.455
-[chief] Yeah. Say cheese. -[Koga] Ready?

421
22:32.081 --> 22:33.290
[camera shutter clicks]

422
22:33.374 --> 22:34.917
[♪ romantic music playing]

423
22:42.132 --> 22:43.133
Well?

424
22:43.217 --> 22:45.302
-[in Korean] There. Ta-da. -[in English] All done?

425
22:45.386 --> 22:46.512
Oh, you're an artist!

426
22:46.595 --> 22:47.721
-Your twin. -Copy paste.

427
22:47.805 --> 22:49.306
-We're twins? -Totally.

428
22:49.390 --> 22:50.683
[both laugh]

429
22:50.766 --> 22:54.103
-[Karin] It's so cute. [chuckles] -[Yubin exclaims]

430
22:54.979 --> 22:57.439
-Oh, wow. [exclaims] -All right,

431
22:57.523 --> 22:58.857
-I'm all done. -[Yubin] Wow.

432
22:58.941 --> 23:01.026
-A heart for you. Thank you. -Thank you.

433
23:01.110 --> 23:02.528
Have a good day.

434
23:02.611 --> 23:04.154
-It's cute. Is that a dog? -Do you like it?

435
23:04.238 --> 23:06.156
-Yeah, it is. -Wow, it's adorable.

436
23:06.240 --> 23:08.450
-One and two. -Here.

437
23:10.619 --> 23:12.621
[no audible dialogue]

438
23:19.044 --> 23:22.214
[chuckles, gasps] Look, flowers.

439
23:22.798 --> 23:24.466
-How pretty. -Hello.

440
23:24.550 --> 23:26.468
-Hi there. -[vendor] Hello.

441
23:38.772 --> 23:39.898
[chuckles]

442
23:50.701 --> 23:51.702
Let's go.

443
23:57.082 --> 23:59.752
-Cheese. -[visitors giggling, exclaiming]

444
23:59.835 --> 24:02.212
Oh, hey. H-H-Hold on, hold on.

445
24:02.296 --> 24:05.549
[visitor] Oh, wow. Hi! Oh!

446
24:05.632 --> 24:08.844
Why are you going over there? Who the heck does he think he is?

447
24:08.927 --> 24:10.554
-I hate his guts. Huh? -Excuse me.

448
24:10.637 --> 24:12.014
Can we take a photo together?

449
24:12.097 --> 24:14.308
-[Kunam] So many of you. -That all right?

450
24:14.933 --> 24:18.270
-Three, two, one, say, "Cheese." -[camera shutter clicks]

451
24:18.353 --> 24:20.105
-Good, thank you. -It's my pleasure.

452
24:20.189 --> 24:22.399
[Kunam] Yeah, that's our social media account.

453
24:22.483 --> 24:24.318
[visitors clamoring]

454
24:24.401 --> 24:25.486
Thank you so much.

455
24:25.569 --> 24:26.987
A sample for you.

456
24:27.071 --> 24:28.280
One for you. Here you are.

457
24:28.363 --> 24:29.782
Thanks for visiting us.

458
24:29.865 --> 24:31.116
-Uh-huh! -[clamoring continues]

459
24:32.326 --> 24:34.328
Why's he got that huge grin on his face?

460
24:34.411 --> 24:36.497
Um, could you take a picture of us?

461
24:37.039 --> 24:39.750
-W-What? -You should be in the photo. Come on.

462
24:39.833 --> 24:41.085
[visitor 1 giggles]

463
24:41.877 --> 24:44.296
-I'm really busy. -[visitor 2] Cheese!

464
24:45.756 --> 24:46.965
[visitor 1] Anyway, uh, okay…

465
24:48.175 --> 24:50.677
-[visitor 3, in Korean] Three, two, one. -[camera shutter clicks]

466
24:50.761 --> 24:52.054
-[in English] It looks good. -[sighs]

467
24:52.137 --> 24:53.639
[visitor 4] Cute. Can I see?

468
24:53.722 --> 24:56.058
[visitor 5 giggles] You have to take another one.

469
24:56.141 --> 24:57.267
[sighs]

470
24:57.351 --> 24:58.727
[Kunam] Sure.

471
25:05.442 --> 25:08.112
IRO ISLAND - CHARO ISLAND AOBA VILLAGE

472
25:12.950 --> 25:14.118
-[child] I see her! -[sighs]

473
25:14.201 --> 25:16.286
-[children exclaiming] -[child] She's right here.

474
25:16.370 --> 25:18.038
-[Karin gasps, chuckles] -We got you a present!

475
25:18.122 --> 25:20.165
[children exclaiming continues]

476
25:20.249 --> 25:22.835
What? Thank you!

477
25:22.918 --> 25:25.963
What? What's all this? [chuckles]

478
25:26.046 --> 25:27.381
You're all so nice.

479
25:27.464 --> 25:29.424
Is your strawberry booth here?

480
25:29.508 --> 25:31.009
It sure is.

481
25:31.093 --> 25:34.429
-This way or that way? -[chuckles]

482
25:34.513 --> 25:35.556
It's over there.

483
25:35.639 --> 25:37.182
-[children exclaiming] -[Karin] Oh!

484
25:37.266 --> 25:39.810
-[chuckles] -[teacher 1] Don't rush.

485
25:41.061 --> 25:42.938
-Thank you. -[teacher 1] Stay together.

486
25:43.564 --> 25:44.815
Take your time.

487
25:47.025 --> 25:48.026
[Karin chuckles]

488
25:48.110 --> 25:49.486
It's been a while.

489
25:49.570 --> 25:50.654
[gasps]

490
25:51.280 --> 25:54.449
Yeah, it really has. It's nice to see you again.

491
25:54.533 --> 25:55.993
What are you doing here?

492
25:56.076 --> 25:57.578
[teacher 2] He asked us to come.

493
25:57.661 --> 25:58.662
[chuckles]

494
25:59.496 --> 26:01.540
[chuckles] Yubin…

495
26:03.584 --> 26:06.795
-You got it. Here, you can do it. Here. -Thank you.

496
26:06.879 --> 26:08.589
-You got this. You can do it. -[child] Wait!

497
26:09.298 --> 26:11.675
-[teacher 2] We'll go visit your booth. -Great, enjoy it.

498
26:11.758 --> 26:14.887
[exclaims, chuckles]

499
26:14.970 --> 26:16.597
-Here's a present for you. -Mmm.

500
26:17.306 --> 26:19.474
-Are you giving me a gift? -[grunts]

501
26:22.436 --> 26:26.148
-[in Korean] Thank you. [grunts, chuckles] -Let's go.

502
26:28.734 --> 26:32.738
[in English] Excuse me. Sorry. Coming through. Please let me through.

503
26:32.821 --> 26:35.115
-[teacher 1] Did you find one? [chuckles] -[children clamoring]

504
26:35.199 --> 26:36.617
Excuse me.

505
26:36.700 --> 26:38.035
Everybody.

506
26:38.785 --> 26:40.120
Excuse me. Sorry.

507
26:40.204 --> 26:42.664
-I brought strawberries for all of you. -[Yubin] Thank you. Behind you.

508
26:42.748 --> 26:45.125
-[child 1] These are so yummy. -[child 2] Can we eat it? Really?

509
26:45.209 --> 26:46.376
Of course you can. Here.

510
26:46.460 --> 26:48.962
-There's enough for everyone, all right? -Can we really have one?

511
26:49.046 --> 26:51.590
-[Karin] Did anybody not get a strawberry? -[in Korean] My goodness.

512
26:52.299 --> 26:54.509
-[in English] Thank you. -Wait, can I get a big one?

513
26:54.593 --> 26:57.387
-[groaning] -[Karin chuckles]

514
26:57.471 --> 27:00.015
[children clamoring]

515
27:02.601 --> 27:04.061
Yummy?

516
27:04.144 --> 27:06.355
-[child 6] A weird green thing's on mine. -[Karin] What?

517
27:06.438 --> 27:08.106
Did everyone get at least one?

518
27:08.190 --> 27:10.234
-Yes. Take that one, hurry. -Where do I put it?

519
27:10.317 --> 27:11.693
I'm putting mine here.

520
27:12.694 --> 27:14.071
Charo Island!

521
27:14.154 --> 27:15.656
Kabocha incoming!

522
27:16.198 --> 27:17.658
Almost there!

523
27:17.741 --> 27:18.909
I'm here!

524
27:18.992 --> 27:20.369
-Want one? -This looks great.

525
27:20.452 --> 27:22.746
-[in Korean] Here, here, here. -[chief, in English] Here, I got it.

526
27:22.829 --> 27:24.665
-[chief] Wow, kabocha pumpkin. -[Yubin straining]

527
27:24.748 --> 27:26.041
-Yubin! Yubin! -Yeah. What's up?

528
27:26.124 --> 27:27.167
Sweet potatoes.

529
27:27.250 --> 27:29.670
-[in Korean] Sweet potatoes. -Sweet potatoes. [in English] Okay.

530
27:29.753 --> 27:31.797
[moderator] The Green Nova Corporation FESTA judges…

531
27:31.880 --> 27:33.840
-…will now begin their round… -Everyone, please vote for us!

532
27:33.924 --> 27:35.384
-…visiting and rating each booth… -Check us out.

533
27:35.467 --> 27:37.678
-…participating in the competition. -Showtime, everybody.

534
27:37.761 --> 27:40.973
[moderator] We ask that each booth has a representative present

535
27:41.056 --> 27:43.266
to greet and attend to the judges.

536
27:44.059 --> 27:45.686
KABOCHA PUMPKIN KARIN'S STRAWBERRIES

537
27:45.769 --> 27:46.770
[Karin] Mm-hmm.

538
27:47.688 --> 27:49.523
-[Yubin, in Korean] All done. -[in English] Good.

539
27:49.606 --> 27:50.732
-Okay. Yes. -Okay.

540
27:52.067 --> 27:55.529
This year's theme is "Oh, so juicy." Say it with me. Ready?

541
27:55.612 --> 27:57.990
-"Oh, so juicy." That was great. -[judges] "Oh, so juicy."

542
27:58.073 --> 27:59.866
[Reiji] I'm sweeping the competition again.

543
27:59.950 --> 28:01.410
Ain't it incredible?

544
28:01.493 --> 28:06.123
Iro Island's tangerines are the most delicious in all of Asia. Here…

545
28:06.206 --> 28:07.207
Want one?

546
28:07.290 --> 28:09.334
-[Reiji] Absolutely. Oh, so juicy! -[Yubin exclaims]

547
28:09.418 --> 28:11.712
[Reiji] Look at the rind. See? It peels right off.

548
28:11.795 --> 28:13.547
[Yubin] Mmm.

549
28:13.630 --> 28:14.631
[chuckles]

550
28:17.092 --> 28:19.094
-Juicy? -Mm-hmm.

551
28:19.177 --> 28:20.429
Mmm. Really good.

552
28:21.013 --> 28:22.556
[in Korean] There's no way we'd lose.

553
28:22.639 --> 28:23.890
[in English] Don't worry.

554
28:23.974 --> 28:25.767
-Mm-hmm. [chuckles] -Everything will work out.

555
28:25.851 --> 28:28.270
[in Korean] Take deep breaths. Come on.

556
28:28.353 --> 28:31.398
-[breathes deeply] -[breathes deeply, chuckles]

557
28:31.481 --> 28:33.483
[breathing deeply]

558
28:35.569 --> 28:36.611
[grunts]

559
28:36.695 --> 28:38.238
-[in English] You got this. -[Karin] Mm-hmm.

560
28:38.321 --> 28:39.906
-Oh. Oh, here they come. -Ah, ah!

561
28:41.700 --> 28:44.327
-It's great to meet you. Hello. -[judge 1] Oh, the pleasure is mine.

562
28:44.411 --> 28:45.704
Thank you for stopping by.

563
28:47.164 --> 28:48.331
Welcome to our booth.

564
28:48.415 --> 28:49.541
Happy to have you.

565
28:49.624 --> 28:52.294
-What a pretty color. -[Karin] Thank you.

566
28:52.377 --> 28:54.171
-Mind if I take one? -Yes, go right ahead.

567
28:54.254 --> 28:56.006
[judge 2] They look so fresh and vibrant. Mmm.

568
28:57.049 --> 29:00.552
I selected the variety most compatible with the air and soil

569
29:00.635 --> 29:03.180
of Charo island, and no green houses were involved.

570
29:03.263 --> 29:05.474
-Grown in the elements of nature? -Whoa.

571
29:06.433 --> 29:08.977
Didn't that make it more difficult?

572
29:09.811 --> 29:12.230
It sure did. It was a lot harder than I thought. [chuckles]

573
29:12.314 --> 29:13.690
-[chuckles] -I admire your honesty.

574
29:13.774 --> 29:14.816
[Karin chuckles]

575
29:14.900 --> 29:17.736
Why are you determined to grow these outdoors?

576
29:17.819 --> 29:20.947
Well, it's because my grandfather inspired me.

577
29:22.449 --> 29:25.035
When I was young, he always said

578
29:25.118 --> 29:27.913
in nature, strawberries ripen with each season,

579
29:27.996 --> 29:30.290
and the seasons will determine their taste.

580
29:31.166 --> 29:35.087
Honestly, learning the rhythms of each season

581
29:35.170 --> 29:37.380
is a bit difficult to determine accurately.

582
29:37.464 --> 29:38.965
It's worth it though.

583
29:39.049 --> 29:41.426
When strawberries are given the freedom to grow,

584
29:41.510 --> 29:43.887
the resulting taste is quite unique.

585
29:43.970 --> 29:47.557
My goal in all this is to master that rhythm for myself.

586
29:48.725 --> 29:50.477
-It's so good. -[chuckles]

587
29:50.560 --> 29:52.062
-Thank you, sir. -[Yubin] Delicious.

588
29:52.145 --> 29:53.939
They're very delicious, yeah.

589
29:54.022 --> 29:55.899
-[Karin chuckles] -The best ones.

590
29:55.982 --> 29:57.818
-[all chuckle] -"Karin's Strawberries."

591
29:57.901 --> 29:58.944
I hope you consider us.

592
29:59.027 --> 30:00.946
[person] It's been quite a while, Karin.

593
30:05.408 --> 30:08.453
-[gasps] Oh, wow, it has. [chuckles] -[person gasps]

594
30:08.537 --> 30:11.248
Look at you. Boy, how you've grown. [chuckles]

595
30:11.331 --> 30:14.167
-[Karin chuckles] -Not only did you grow up well,

596
30:14.251 --> 30:15.585
you're a participant today.

597
30:15.669 --> 30:17.045
It's so nice to see you.

598
30:17.671 --> 30:20.799
I heard through the grapevine that you joined the Green Nova Corporation,

599
30:20.882 --> 30:22.843
but I never imagined I'd run into you here.

600
30:22.926 --> 30:25.470
Thanks to that, we're able to meet again.

601
30:25.554 --> 30:27.389
-[chuckles] Ah. -[chuckles]

602
30:29.808 --> 30:30.976
Oh, please.

603
30:33.562 --> 30:34.729
[person grunts]

604
30:46.158 --> 30:47.534
Ah… [chuckles]

605
30:49.494 --> 30:51.788
If you have documents related to these strawberries,

606
30:51.872 --> 30:53.707
will you please email then to me when you can?

607
30:53.790 --> 30:54.916
[Karin] Of course.

608
30:55.000 --> 30:56.626
I have an information pack all written up,

609
30:56.710 --> 30:58.461
so I'll send it to you after I wrap up today.

610
30:58.545 --> 30:59.671
-Thank you. -Sure.

611
30:59.754 --> 31:03.842
Well, if anything comes up, reach out.

612
31:06.803 --> 31:08.013
Thank you very much.

613
31:08.096 --> 31:10.432
-It's been a pleasure. [chuckles] -[Karin] I agree.

614
31:11.349 --> 31:12.517
[grunts, chuckles]

615
31:16.605 --> 31:18.899
-[Karin sighs] -[Yubin grunts]

616
31:18.982 --> 31:21.276
-Did I do okay? -Yes. You did great.

617
31:21.359 --> 31:22.694
-It was perfect. -[chuckles]

618
31:22.777 --> 31:25.113
-[sighs] Oh, I was nervous. -You're amazing. Yeah.

619
31:26.448 --> 31:29.117
-So, uh, that… -Mmm.

620
31:29.201 --> 31:32.704
-…last guy. Who was that? A vendor? -Hmm? Mmm.

621
31:32.787 --> 31:34.122
Uh…

622
31:34.206 --> 31:35.498
He's just…

623
31:35.582 --> 31:37.000
-this man that… -[Yubin] Mm-hmm?

624
31:37.083 --> 31:38.376
…used to visit when I was little.

625
31:38.460 --> 31:40.545
-Uh-huh. -He would drop by all the time,

626
31:40.629 --> 31:43.048
-and he was always really kind to us. -Ah.

627
31:43.924 --> 31:45.717
The strawberries are marvelous.

628
31:49.221 --> 31:51.181
Is that man competing as well?

629
31:51.264 --> 31:55.268
Oh, he's probably a friend or booth staff that she hired.

630
31:55.769 --> 32:00.148
Let's see if he's registered on the pre-event application file…

631
32:01.775 --> 32:03.735
I'm terribly sorry, sir, but I'm afraid

632
32:03.818 --> 32:06.571
I don't see him listed as a participating farmer anywhere.

633
32:07.530 --> 32:10.450
[grunts] This isn't acceptable in the slightest.

634
32:10.533 --> 32:13.411
I'm to be informed of all goings-on at Green Nova events,

635
32:13.495 --> 32:14.746
-and I wasn't. -I…

636
32:15.538 --> 32:16.665
My apologies.

637
32:17.290 --> 32:20.377
I will confirm who he is and report back immediately.

638
32:23.546 --> 32:26.216
-The similarity is uncanny. -[Karin] Please try a sample.

639
32:26.299 --> 32:28.593
-Here you go. Thank you. -Thanks for stopping by. Oh.

640
32:28.677 --> 32:30.262
Of course, we have plenty left.

641
32:31.930 --> 32:34.849
Ladies and gentlemen, it is now time

642
32:34.933 --> 32:39.062
to announce the Green Nova Corporation sixth annual FESTA event winners.

643
32:39.145 --> 32:40.647
[cheering]

644
32:40.730 --> 32:44.985
[emcee] The Green Nova Corporation FESTA's very own handpicked judging panel

645
32:45.068 --> 32:46.945
evaluated all of the products…

646
32:47.028 --> 32:48.697
[♪ dramatic music playing]

647
32:49.531 --> 32:52.033
…as well as the booth operations.

648
32:57.038 --> 33:00.333
Booth of the Day was voted on by Festa attendees.

649
33:00.417 --> 33:05.088
The region with the highest total number of points will be crowned the winner.

650
33:06.256 --> 33:11.011
In addition, Green Nova Corporation will be providing all the support necessary

651
33:11.094 --> 33:15.140
to distribute the winning region's products nationwide!

652
33:15.223 --> 33:17.767
Which region will come out on top this year

653
33:17.851 --> 33:20.562
and take home the award of a lifetime?

654
33:20.645 --> 33:22.063
[crowd cheering]

655
33:24.190 --> 33:27.527
First up, product evaluation.

656
33:27.610 --> 33:31.448
It was a close call, but the winner of this category is…

657
33:33.783 --> 33:34.909
Iro Island!

658
33:34.993 --> 33:39.080
-Yeah! [cheering] -[cheering]

659
33:39.164 --> 33:44.252
[fans chanting] Reiji, Reiji!

660
33:44.336 --> 33:46.004
-[sighs] -[emcee] Things are heating up.

661
33:46.504 --> 33:48.089
Reiji, Reiji!

662
33:49.215 --> 33:51.718
-Yeah! -The next category is booth operation.

663
33:52.302 --> 33:56.306
Various regional groups have created entertaining booth designs and operations,

664
33:56.389 --> 33:57.724
charming the guests.

665
33:58.308 --> 34:00.769
And the booth operations category winner is…

666
34:00.852 --> 34:03.229
I got this. Yeah.

667
34:03.313 --> 34:05.440
[♪ competitive music plays]

668
34:08.360 --> 34:09.694
Charo Island!

669
34:09.778 --> 34:11.946
[crowd applauding, cheering]

670
34:12.697 --> 34:14.532
[♪ triumphant music playing]

671
34:17.369 --> 34:22.123
[emcee] Now this, ladies and gentlemen, is the moment you've all been waiting for.

672
34:22.207 --> 34:23.500
The highest combined score,

673
34:23.583 --> 34:27.087
including the points from the category that carries the most weight,

674
34:27.170 --> 34:28.171
Booth of the Day,

675
34:28.254 --> 34:30.173
will be crowned Festa winner.

676
34:31.257 --> 34:34.094
-Everyone… -[sighs]

677
34:34.928 --> 34:36.971
…are you all ready?

678
34:37.597 --> 34:39.015
The Sixth…

679
34:40.850 --> 34:44.813
Green Nova Corporation FESTA winner is…

680
34:45.397 --> 34:47.690
[drum roll]

681
34:57.826 --> 34:58.910
[drum roll stops]

682
34:58.993 --> 35:00.370
[emcee] Charo Island!

683
35:00.453 --> 35:02.247
[crowd cheering]

684
35:03.289 --> 35:05.583
[♪ cheerful pop music playing]

685
35:10.839 --> 35:13.216
-[Mari] Karin! -Karin!

686
35:13.299 --> 35:16.010
[Mari] Karin! [laughing]

687
35:17.679 --> 35:23.017
[exclaims, in Korean] We won! We won this thing!

688
35:23.560 --> 35:25.061
[emcee, in English] The award will be presented

689
35:25.145 --> 35:28.398
by a Green Nova Corporation Festa representative.

690
35:29.107 --> 35:32.193
Charo Island's booth representative, please step forward.

691
35:32.277 --> 35:33.903
[chuckling, cheering]

692
35:40.326 --> 35:42.662
-Congratulations. -Thank you so much.

693
35:48.918 --> 35:50.837
[crowd cheers]

694
35:54.257 --> 35:57.761
[emcee] We will now hear a few words from Charo Island's booth representative,

695
35:57.844 --> 35:59.262
Shirahama Karin.

696
35:59.345 --> 36:00.597
Take it away.

697
36:03.475 --> 36:07.145
I'm Shirahama Karin, and I'm representing Charo Island.

698
36:07.228 --> 36:10.565
I feel incredibly honored to receive this award.

699
36:10.648 --> 36:13.026
Our strawberries, kabocha, and sweet potatoes

700
36:13.109 --> 36:16.362
are grown with love and effort on Charo Island's soil.

701
36:16.446 --> 36:18.323
And I am so thrilled to be acknowledged.

702
36:18.406 --> 36:20.909
Today's victory means so much,

703
36:21.701 --> 36:24.120
as this Festa has given us an opportunity

704
36:24.204 --> 36:28.082
for people all over Japan to enjoy our produce.

705
36:28.166 --> 36:31.085
This has always been a dream of mine.

706
36:32.378 --> 36:35.381
Charo Island's residents, myself included,

707
36:35.465 --> 36:37.759
will do our very best.

708
36:37.842 --> 36:41.471
We'll create products that will be cherished and enjoyed by all.

709
36:42.347 --> 36:44.307
Thank you again for this great honor.

710
36:44.390 --> 36:45.892
[crowd cheers]

711
36:48.311 --> 36:49.813
[Mari] Yay, Karin!

712
36:55.568 --> 36:57.320
-[emcee] Thank you, Ms. Shirahama. -[Karin] Thank you.

713
36:57.403 --> 36:59.489
DO YOU KNOW HOW LONG IT'S BEEN? CALL ME.

714
36:59.572 --> 37:02.867
All right, everyone. This now concludes the Sixth Green Nova Corporation Festa.

715
37:02.951 --> 37:05.161
Thank you all for participating and coming out.

716
37:05.245 --> 37:07.622
-[sighs] -Please get home safely.

717
37:43.157 --> 37:44.742
-[villager chuckles] -Thanks so much, everyone.

718
37:44.826 --> 37:47.120
[all chattering, chuckling]

719
37:47.203 --> 37:48.371
Congratulations!

720
37:48.913 --> 37:52.625
-[chief] Great work today, everyone. -[Karin] Nice teamwork!

721
37:52.709 --> 37:54.752
Hey, check out the trophy we won.

722
37:54.836 --> 37:56.379
Ah, so wonderful!

723
37:56.462 --> 37:58.548
-Yay! -[chief] It's gonna bring us good luck.

724
37:58.631 --> 38:00.216
[villager] Yeah! [chuckling]

725
38:00.842 --> 38:03.636
[chief] It's only up from here. Good things are coming.

726
38:05.388 --> 38:07.974
[♪ pensive music playing]

727
38:10.101 --> 38:13.229
[no audible dialogue]

728
38:21.237 --> 38:23.114
We're gonna win! [cheers]

729
38:28.661 --> 38:30.079
-Yubin. -[Yubin] Yeah.

730
38:32.040 --> 38:33.666
You worked hard today too.

731
38:33.750 --> 38:34.751
Ah.

732
38:41.883 --> 38:44.135
Mmm. It was fun.

733
38:44.218 --> 38:45.887
Mm-hmm, it really was.

734
38:48.681 --> 38:51.267
[in Korean] Hey, so apparently,

735
38:51.351 --> 38:53.478
there's going to be fireworks nearby.

736
38:53.561 --> 38:55.313
[stammers, in English] The big fireworks.

737
38:55.396 --> 38:56.940
-Ah. -Mm-hmm.

738
38:57.023 --> 38:59.817
-[in Korean] You want to see? -[in English] Uh-huh. Mmm, yeah.

739
38:59.901 --> 39:01.861
-Let's do it. -Huh, really?

740
39:01.945 --> 39:03.696
-[in Korean] Let's go. Yeah. -Really?

741
39:10.161 --> 39:13.665
It's so crowded. [chuckles]

742
39:16.626 --> 39:17.835
Mmm…

743
39:19.170 --> 39:22.924
[in English] Uh, it's a lot… [chuckles] …Crowded.

744
39:25.301 --> 39:26.761
-Hey. This way. -Hmm? Huh?

745
39:26.844 --> 39:28.262
-Here. Come with me. -Oh. Wait.

746
39:28.346 --> 39:30.056
-[stammers] Sorry. -Sorry.

747
39:30.139 --> 39:32.392
-[in Korean] Where are we going? -[in English] Over here. This way. Here.

748
39:32.475 --> 39:35.395
-Hurry. Excuse us. -[in Korean] Wait. Wait.

749
39:37.313 --> 39:38.606
[in English] Wow.

750
39:39.107 --> 39:41.109
-Here, here… -Hmm?

751
39:41.192 --> 39:44.278
-It's nice, it's quiet. Uh-huh. -Mm-hmm. Right.

752
39:45.488 --> 39:46.572
[chuckles]

753
39:47.240 --> 39:49.534
[in Korean] Perfect spot for zoning out.

754
39:50.660 --> 39:51.869
-Hmm? -Huh?

755
39:52.829 --> 39:55.039
[in English] "Hit the bruise"? What is that?

756
39:55.123 --> 39:57.375
-A bruise? -[in Korean] The translation is incorrect.

757
39:58.209 --> 40:01.421
"Zoning out" is when…

758
40:01.504 --> 40:05.258
You're just so overwhelmed.

759
40:05.341 --> 40:07.051
It's like letting your mind go blank

760
40:07.135 --> 40:09.762
when you don't want to think about anything.

761
40:11.556 --> 40:12.932
Ah. [chuckles]

762
40:13.516 --> 40:15.977
[in English] Ah. Mmm, I get it.

763
40:17.645 --> 40:20.023
It's important to have your own special spot,

764
40:20.106 --> 40:22.984
someplace all to yourself when you're feeling overwhelmed.

765
40:23.609 --> 40:25.820
-Do you have somewhere like that? -Mm-hmm.

766
40:27.697 --> 40:28.906
[in Korean] For me…

767
40:30.575 --> 40:32.702
-This place. -[in English] Wow.

768
40:33.619 --> 40:35.246
That's nice.

769
40:35.329 --> 40:36.873
-[in Korean] Isn't it pretty? -Ooh.

770
40:36.956 --> 40:41.085
This is where I go when things get really tough.

771
40:41.753 --> 40:44.464
If you ever come to Seoul, I'll take you there.

772
40:45.757 --> 40:47.759
[in English] Mmm, sounds good to me.

773
41:06.444 --> 41:08.029
In all honesty,

774
41:08.654 --> 41:11.324
I've never been anywhere outside of Japan.

775
41:14.494 --> 41:16.537
[in Korean] Oh. Seriously?

776
41:17.163 --> 41:18.164
Mmm.

777
41:19.749 --> 41:22.502
[in English] There are lots of things I've never gotten to try

778
41:22.585 --> 41:23.836
because of my condition.

779
41:27.632 --> 41:29.801
This is my first time doing this,

780
41:30.468 --> 41:32.678
walking around, exploring the city with someone.

781
41:34.514 --> 41:37.725
Truthfully, I'll probably never even have a boyfriend.

782
41:40.478 --> 41:41.729
[in Korean] Why not?

783
41:42.438 --> 41:44.941
[in English] Anytime I get excited my body collapses.

784
41:46.192 --> 41:48.027
I collapse when my heart pounds too much.

785
41:49.821 --> 41:52.198
[sighs] Just holding hands can make me…

786
42:01.207 --> 42:02.667
[in Korean] What else do you want to do?

787
42:10.258 --> 42:11.592
[in English] Fall in love.

788
42:24.397 --> 42:25.398
[in Korean] I like you.

789
42:46.460 --> 42:48.713
[♪ upbeat music playing]

790
43:17.200 --> 43:19.493
MERRY BERRY LOVE

791
43:19.577 --> 43:20.578
NEXT EPISODE

792
43:20.661 --> 43:22.496
[Karin] "For Koreans, there are steps before romance."

793
43:22.580 --> 43:25.082
What is our relationship, exactly?

794
43:25.166 --> 43:26.417
[in Korean] Is that you, Yubin?

795
43:27.793 --> 43:30.546
[Karin, in English] What's the real reason you came to this island?
